#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/clone.md:36
msgid "\"String\""
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/clone.md:43
msgid "// Copies the reference-counted pointer, not the value.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/clone.md:50
msgid ""
"\"Deep copy\" a value, or in the case of reference counting pointers like "
"`Rc`/`Arc` create a new instance of that pointer."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/foundations-api-design/predictable-api/common-traits/clone.md:53
msgid ""
"When to not implement/derive: For types that, to maintain an invariant, the "
"value should not be duplicated. We'll touch on this later in Idiomatic Rust."
msgstr ""
